## Method

Every arm processes the same input bytes. Warm-up runs come first, then timed
runs; we report medians with ninety-five percent percentile-bootstrap
confidence intervals,
at one thread (`t1`) and at all vCPUs (`tN`). A **speed-up** is the baseline
median divided by the candidate median, so above parity means the candidate is
faster. When the interval contains parity we say **no measurable difference**,
whatever the point estimate. Operations are grouped into **KleidiCV-listed**
operations (the ones COOL can accelerate on Arm), **control** operations
(OpenCV calls without KleidiCV kernels) and a **NumPy negative control** that
COOL cannot touch.

